WEBVTT

00:00:00.131 --> 00:00:19.612
Canterbury Tales Geoffrey Chaucer Teen Ailey Readers Copyright Ailey 2014 Chapter 1 The Prologue It's a beautiful day.

00:00:19.672 --> 00:00:27.492
The weather is good, the birds are singing, the grass is green and there are flowers everywhere.

00:00:27.553 --> 00:00:31.291
Now, my story can begin.

00:00:31.351 --> 00:00:39.508
My name's Jeffrey, and today I'm going on a pilgrimage to Canterbury.

00:00:39.567 --> 00:00:43.391
I'm going to Canterbury with a group of people.

00:00:43.451 --> 00:00:46.034
We're going there together.

00:00:46.094 --> 00:00:52.318
I met these people yesterday at an inn in London.

00:00:52.378 --> 00:00:56.532
I arrived at the inn in the afternoon.

00:00:56.592 --> 00:01:00.695
I was very tired and hungry.

00:01:00.754 --> 00:01:08.181
Good afternoon, I said to the man who worked at the inn, he was the innkeeper.

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:10.982
I'd like a room for the night.

00:01:11.042 --> 00:01:13.696
I'm going to Canterbury tomorrow.

00:01:13.756 --> 00:01:16.148
The road to Canterbury is long.

00:01:16.208 --> 00:01:20.030
I need to sleep well before I start.

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:23.908
Good afternoon, said the innkeeper.

00:01:23.968 --> 00:01:28.024
Do you know that some other people are going to Canterbury tomorrow?

00:01:28.084 --> 00:01:30.797
They're staying here tonight.

00:01:30.856 --> 00:01:35.790
I'd like to meet them, I said to the innkeeper.

00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:40.274
In the evening, I met the other people.

00:01:40.334 --> 00:01:46.038
The inn was big, and there was a lot of good food and drink.

00:01:46.098 --> 00:01:53.611
Everybody had dinner together, and the innkeeper gave good food to everybody.

00:01:53.671 --> 00:01:56.902
The innkeeper was a nice person.

00:01:56.962 --> 00:02:02.046
He was a very big man, and he enjoyed speaking to people.

00:02:02.105 --> 00:02:05.388
He was very good at his job.

00:02:05.447 --> 00:02:09.330
Everybody enjoyed their dinner.

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:15.044
After dinner, the innkeeper spoke to the group.

00:02:15.104 --> 00:02:19.968
You're a very nice group of people, he said.

00:02:20.028 --> 00:02:23.834
I know that God will listen to your prayers.

00:02:23.894 --> 00:02:27.109
You're all going to the same place.

00:02:27.169 --> 00:02:30.592
So you must go to Canterbury together.

00:02:30.652 --> 00:02:32.434
What do you think?

00:02:32.493 --> 00:02:37.156
Yes, we can go together, I said.

00:02:37.216 --> 00:02:42.540
And I want to go to Canterbury with you, said the innkeeper.

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:47.864
Now, we have to travel for a long time.

00:02:47.924 --> 00:02:52.326
And I think we can do something interesting.

00:02:52.386 --> 00:02:54.786
We can play a game.

00:02:54.846 --> 00:02:56.646
What do you think?

00:02:56.706 --> 00:03:00.348
Yes, said everybody in the group.

00:03:00.408 --> 00:03:02.898
Tell us about this game.

00:03:02.958 --> 00:03:08.700
Now, listen to what I have to say, said the innkeeper.

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:16.462
We'll go to Canterbury together and every person will tell a story.

00:03:16.522 --> 00:03:25.155
I'll listen to every story, then I'll tell you which story is the best.

00:03:25.215 --> 00:03:30.157
Everybody in the group wanted to play this game.

00:03:30.217 --> 00:03:39.610
Very well, said the innkeeper, and I will give something to the person who tells the best story.

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:46.849
That person will have dinner at my inn, and I'll pay for the dinner.

00:03:46.909 --> 00:03:55.890
The people in the group were very happy, and they began to think of what story to tell.

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:59.732
In the group, there was a knight.

00:03:59.791 --> 00:04:06.456
Everybody liked him, and he was always happy to help people.

00:04:06.516 --> 00:04:11.989
He was an important man, but his clothes were cheap.

00:04:12.048 --> 00:04:17.391
His horse was fast, but it was small.

00:04:17.450 --> 00:04:24.602
I'm a knight, and my life is very exciting, said the knight.

00:04:24.662 --> 00:04:29.024
And my story is also going to be exciting.

00:04:29.084 --> 00:04:34.617
It's about two brothers who love the same woman.

00:04:34.676 --> 00:04:38.718
There was also a clerk in the group.

00:04:38.778 --> 00:04:44.010
He was a nice man, but he didn't speak very much.

00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:47.462
He liked reading and studying.

00:04:47.522 --> 00:04:50.334
That's all he wanted to do.

00:04:50.393 --> 00:04:55.628
He was very slim, and he didn't eat very much.

00:04:55.688 --> 00:05:00.260
And he liked books more than food.

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:05.674
I read a lot of books, said the Clark.

00:05:05.734 --> 00:05:10.438
I don't want nice clothes, or good food.

00:05:10.498 --> 00:05:13.170
I don't have much money.

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:17.590
And I use the money I have to buy books.

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:22.000
That's why I read a lot of stories.

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:29.906
My story is very easy to understand, but it's not boring.

00:05:29.965 --> 00:05:32.878
I think everybody will enjoy it.

00:05:32.938 --> 00:05:38.402
It's about a king who has many secrets.

00:05:38.462 --> 00:05:43.426
Another person in the group was a merchant.

00:05:43.486 --> 00:05:46.434
He had a lot of money.

00:05:46.494 --> 00:05:49.584
But he wasn't a happy man.

00:05:49.643 --> 00:05:53.476
He always had a sad face.

00:05:53.536 --> 00:05:57.069
He was different from the night.

00:05:57.129 --> 00:06:00.552
His clothes were very expensive.

00:06:00.612 --> 00:06:03.124
Everything he had was expensive.

00:06:03.184 --> 00:06:07.838
His clothes, his hat, and his horse.

00:06:07.898 --> 00:06:13.082
I have an important business, said the merchant.

00:06:13.141 --> 00:06:16.497
And I have a lot of things to do.

00:06:16.557 --> 00:06:20.500
But I'm not very happy with my life.

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:25.032
And that's why my story will be said.

00:06:25.092 --> 00:06:29.052
It'll be about an old man who can't see.

00:06:29.072 --> 00:06:35.263
I also have to tell you about another man.

00:06:35.323 --> 00:06:37.844
He was a Franklin.

00:06:37.904 --> 00:06:40.684
He was different from the Clark.

00:06:40.744 --> 00:06:46.108
He was very rich and important, but he didn't have a business.

00:06:46.167 --> 00:06:53.124
He had a big house in the country, and he often invited people there.

00:06:53.184 --> 00:06:55.224
He liked good food.

00:06:55.245 --> 00:07:01.618
"'I'm very old, and my house is big.

00:07:01.678 --> 00:07:06.770
And I like inviting people there,' said the Franklin.

00:07:06.830 --> 00:07:10.933
In my house I often tell stories.

00:07:10.993 --> 00:07:12.984
I enjoy it.

00:07:13.044 --> 00:07:16.712
My story will be very interesting.

00:07:16.772 --> 00:07:21.402
It's about a woman who doesn't like the sea.

00:07:21.462 --> 00:07:24.694
Why doesn't she like the sea?

00:07:24.754 --> 00:07:29.918
Well, you'll have to listen to my story.

00:07:29.978 --> 00:07:34.642
There is another person I want to tell you about.

00:07:34.701 --> 00:07:37.224
He was a gardener.

00:07:37.284 --> 00:07:40.006
He also liked reading.

00:07:40.066 --> 00:07:44.309
And he liked to sing songs and say prayers.

00:07:44.368 --> 00:07:48.419
He had a strange face.

00:07:48.479 --> 00:07:56.408
I travel a lot, and I always say prayers for people," said the partner.

00:07:56.468 --> 00:08:00.549
There are a lot of bad people in the world.

00:08:00.609 --> 00:08:06.820
I'll say a prayer for them, but they have to give me some money.

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:14.631
My story will be about three people who do something very bad.

00:08:14.691 --> 00:08:17.532
Everybody was tired.

00:08:17.592 --> 00:08:19.829
It was late in the evening.

00:08:19.889 --> 00:08:27.732
and the night said, we can go to bed now, then we can leave early in the morning.

00:08:27.792 --> 00:08:30.535
We all went to bed.

00:08:30.594 --> 00:08:34.918
We were tired but happy.

00:08:34.978 --> 00:08:43.356
Early next morning we got up and then we left for Canterbury on our horses.

00:08:43.415 --> 00:08:46.098
We were slow.

00:08:46.158 --> 00:08:53.982
and after many hours we came to a place called St. Thomas, and we stopped there.

00:08:54.042 --> 00:08:59.664
We sat down, and then we had something to eat.

00:08:59.724 --> 00:09:08.066
After eating, the innkeeper said, listen, do you remember what we said last night?

00:09:08.126 --> 00:09:11.434
Of course, said the night.

00:09:11.494 --> 00:09:16.823
Well, said the innkeeper, who wants to begin?

00:09:16.883 --> 00:09:20.926
Who wants to tell the first story?

00:09:20.986 --> 00:09:25.628
I'm happy to tell you my story, said the night.

00:09:25.688 --> 00:09:27.930
I think you'll enjoy it.

00:09:27.990 --> 00:09:31.202
It's very exciting.

00:09:31.262 --> 00:09:37.156
And then the night began to tell his story.

00:09:37.216 --> 00:09:49.754
Chapter 2 The Knight's Tale My story is about two brothers, said the Knight.

00:09:49.814 --> 00:09:55.295
Their names were Palamon and Arcyte, and they were knights.

00:09:55.355 --> 00:09:59.326
The brothers were from a city called Thebes.

00:09:59.386 --> 00:10:02.446
They did everything together.

00:10:02.506 --> 00:10:06.897
They weren't only brothers, they were also friends.

00:10:06.958 --> 00:10:10.351
But they were very sad.

00:10:10.411 --> 00:10:15.175
They were sad because they didn't live in thebes anymore.

00:10:15.235 --> 00:10:17.766
They lived in Athens.

00:10:17.826 --> 00:10:20.606
And they didn't live in a house.

00:10:20.666 --> 00:10:23.566
They lived in a prison.

00:10:23.626 --> 00:10:29.508
They couldn't leave the prison, and they couldn't speak to anybody.

00:10:29.568 --> 00:10:34.449
Every morning, they looked out of the prison window.

00:10:34.509 --> 00:10:41.152
From their window, they could see a beautiful garden.

00:10:41.212 --> 00:10:48.798
One morning, Palamon woke up and then he looked out of the window.

00:10:48.858 --> 00:10:51.980
But something was different.

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:55.272
There was a woman in the garden.

00:10:55.332 --> 00:10:58.144
Her name was Emily.

00:10:58.204 --> 00:11:02.846
She was the daughter of the King of Athens.

00:11:02.906 --> 00:11:06.189
Look, said Palamon.

00:11:06.249 --> 00:11:09.370
That woman is beautiful.

00:11:09.430 --> 00:11:12.694
Oh, I'm in love.

00:11:12.754 --> 00:11:15.486
Arcyte, come here.

00:11:15.546 --> 00:11:17.346
Look!

00:11:17.406 --> 00:11:23.668
Arcyte went to the window, and he saw the woman.

00:11:23.728 --> 00:11:26.518
Yes, you're right.

00:11:26.578 --> 00:11:30.990
She is beautiful, he said.

00:11:31.050 --> 00:11:35.170
One day I'll marry her.

00:11:35.230 --> 00:11:38.922
I saw her first, said Palamon.

00:11:38.982 --> 00:11:41.127
You can't love her.

00:11:41.187 --> 00:11:43.972
You must help me."

00:11:44.032 --> 00:11:47.124
No, said Arcyte.

00:11:47.184 --> 00:11:50.024
My love is perfect.

00:11:50.084 --> 00:11:53.406
You must help me.

00:11:53.466 --> 00:12:02.208
Arcyte and Panaman both loved Emily, and they had the same conversation every day.

00:12:02.228 --> 00:12:04.909
I love her.

00:12:04.969 --> 00:12:12.772
Now you can't love her, was all you could hear from the small room their prism.

00:12:12.832 --> 00:12:19.766
And then one day, a friend of Arcytes visited the King of Athens.

00:12:19.826 --> 00:12:24.149
He wanted to speak to the King about Arcyte.

00:12:24.209 --> 00:12:26.420
Can he go home?

00:12:26.480 --> 00:12:28.932
Asked Arcyte's friend.

00:12:28.992 --> 00:12:34.364
He's a good man, and I want to see him again.

00:12:34.424 --> 00:12:38.047
I'll do what you ask, said the king.

00:12:38.067 --> 00:12:49.647
Our sight can go home, but he must never come to Athens again, and Palamon must stay in prison.

00:12:49.707 --> 00:12:55.912
Our sight went back to Thebes, but he wasn't happy.

00:12:55.972 --> 00:13:02.390
I'm going home, thought our sight, but I can't see Emily.

00:13:02.450 --> 00:13:05.842
Palamon can see her in the garden.

00:13:05.902 --> 00:13:09.114
It's better in prison.

00:13:09.175 --> 00:13:13.456
But Palamon was sad as well.

00:13:13.516 --> 00:13:19.020
Our sight, you can go back to Athens, he thought.

00:13:19.080 --> 00:13:24.504
You can fight the king of Athens and you can marry Emily.

00:13:24.564 --> 00:13:28.842
I have to stay in this prison.

00:13:28.902 --> 00:13:33.881
In Thebes, our sight was very sad.

00:13:33.941 --> 00:13:37.702
He didn't sleep or eat very much.

00:13:37.762 --> 00:13:42.244
I'll wait for two years, thought our sight.

00:13:42.304 --> 00:13:45.524
And then I'll go to Athens again.

00:13:45.584 --> 00:13:47.735
Nobody will know me.

00:13:47.795 --> 00:13:50.346
I'll wear different clothes.

00:13:50.406 --> 00:13:52.306
I'll change my name.

00:13:52.366 --> 00:13:55.157
And I'll find a job.

00:13:55.217 --> 00:13:59.070
I'll be a servant in the King's house.

00:13:59.130 --> 00:14:03.323
And then I'll see Emily.

00:14:03.383 --> 00:14:10.557
And that's why, after two years, our sight went back to Athens.

00:14:10.617 --> 00:14:14.500
And soon he was the king's servant.

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:19.912
The king liked our sight because he was good at his job.

00:14:19.972 --> 00:14:25.556
One day, our sight went to a forest near Athens.

00:14:25.616 --> 00:14:28.612
And he sat near a tree.

00:14:28.672 --> 00:14:30.898
What can I do?"

00:14:30.958 --> 00:14:32.700
said our sight.

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:35.242
I'm the king's servant.

00:14:35.301 --> 00:14:37.462
I'm near Emily.

00:14:37.522 --> 00:14:40.666
But she doesn't know who I am.

00:14:40.726 --> 00:14:44.098
I want to die.

00:14:44.158 --> 00:14:49.132
Then a man spoke to our sight.

00:14:49.192 --> 00:14:51.964
It was Palamon.

00:14:52.024 --> 00:14:54.375
Hello, brother.

00:14:54.435 --> 00:14:57.415
It's me, said Palamon.

00:14:57.475 --> 00:15:00.534
Stop thinking about Emily.

00:15:00.594 --> 00:15:03.705
Only I can love her.

00:15:03.765 --> 00:15:08.196
Parliament, it's you, said Arcyte.

00:15:08.256 --> 00:15:10.678
Why aren't you in prison?

00:15:10.738 --> 00:15:14.008
The king sent me home yesterday.

00:15:14.068 --> 00:15:16.750
But I'm not going home.

00:15:16.810 --> 00:15:19.910
I want to find Emily.

00:15:19.970 --> 00:15:25.162
Well, I'll fight you for Emily, said Arcyte.

00:15:25.222 --> 00:15:26.910
But not today.

00:15:26.970 --> 00:15:29.108
We are knights, remember?

00:15:29.168 --> 00:15:32.240
We must do things in the right way.

00:15:32.300 --> 00:15:39.956
Tonight, I'll bring some food, and then tomorrow we'll fight.

00:15:40.016 --> 00:15:46.660
All right, said Palamon, and so the brothers said goodbye.

00:15:46.720 --> 00:15:55.118
On the next day, they met in the forest, and then they started fighting.

00:15:55.178 --> 00:16:00.746
On the same day, the king was also in the forest.

00:16:00.806 --> 00:16:03.426
He was with Emily.

00:16:03.486 --> 00:16:07.340
And he saw Panaman and Arcyte.

00:16:07.400 --> 00:16:10.312
Stop, said the king.

00:16:10.372 --> 00:16:12.083
What are you doing?

00:16:12.143 --> 00:16:14.464
Stop now.

00:16:14.524 --> 00:16:17.807
Kill us, said Arcyte.

00:16:17.867 --> 00:16:20.459
Now I'm your servant.

00:16:20.518 --> 00:16:24.136
And before that, I was in your prison.

00:16:24.196 --> 00:16:30.536
My name is Arcyte, and this is my brother Palamon.

00:16:30.596 --> 00:16:36.089
We're fighting because we both love Emily.

00:16:36.148 --> 00:16:41.281
Then you must die, said the king.

00:16:41.342 --> 00:16:45.204
But Emily stopped the king.

00:16:45.264 --> 00:16:49.076
Please don't kill them, she said.

00:16:49.136 --> 00:16:52.352
They're fighting for love.

00:16:52.412 --> 00:16:58.488
Well, said the king, you're right, Emily.

00:16:58.548 --> 00:17:02.289
But only one of them can marry you.

00:17:02.349 --> 00:17:07.591
Paloban, our side, come back to the forest next summer.

00:17:07.651 --> 00:17:10.642
Bring a hundred nights.

00:17:10.702 --> 00:17:14.334
And then you'll fight for Emily.

00:17:14.393 --> 00:17:15.504
Now go.

00:17:15.564 --> 00:17:20.138
Soon it was summer.

00:17:20.198 --> 00:17:24.453
Palamon and Arcyte came back to Athens.

00:17:24.514 --> 00:17:31.608
They both had a hundred knights and they were ready to fight the next day.

00:17:31.668 --> 00:17:36.402
That night, Palamon had a dream.

00:17:36.462 --> 00:17:42.236
In his dream, a woman said, I can see you.

00:17:42.296 --> 00:17:45.908
You are marrying Emily.

00:17:45.968 --> 00:17:51.078
On the same night, Arcyte also had a dream.

00:17:51.138 --> 00:17:56.788
In his dream, a man said, I can hear you.

00:17:56.848 --> 00:18:03.693
You are saying, Hooray, Emily will be my wife.

00:18:03.753 --> 00:18:07.156
Which dream was right?

00:18:07.216 --> 00:18:11.668
Well, now I'll tell you.

00:18:11.729 --> 00:18:16.652
In the morning, everybody came to the forest.

00:18:16.712 --> 00:18:21.622
The nights were ready and they began to fight.

00:18:21.682 --> 00:18:26.411
After three hours, Emily was worried.

00:18:26.471 --> 00:18:29.412
They're fighting for me.

00:18:29.472 --> 00:18:32.324
Who's going to be my husband?

00:18:32.384 --> 00:18:34.796
When will they stop?

00:18:34.856 --> 00:18:40.138
And then, after many hours, they did stop.

00:18:40.198 --> 00:18:43.570
Palamon was very tired.

00:18:43.630 --> 00:18:46.120
Stop, he said.

00:18:46.180 --> 00:18:49.304
I can't fight anymore.

00:18:49.364 --> 00:18:53.136
Stop fighting, said the king.

00:18:53.196 --> 00:18:56.588
Our sight will be Emily's husband.

00:18:56.648 --> 00:19:00.169
Hooray, said our sight.

00:19:00.229 --> 00:19:02.550
I'm very happy.

00:19:02.610 --> 00:19:05.521
Emily will be my wife.

00:19:05.581 --> 00:19:08.562
I must go to her and...

00:19:08.622 --> 00:19:13.334
But then, our sight stopped speaking.

00:19:13.394 --> 00:19:16.984
He didn't feel very well.

00:19:17.044 --> 00:19:21.084
People came to help our sight.

00:19:21.144 --> 00:19:25.276
I'm not well, said our sight.

00:19:25.336 --> 00:19:30.538
I can't, I can't feel anything.

00:19:30.598 --> 00:19:32.838
I'm dying.

00:19:32.898 --> 00:19:35.410
This is the end.

00:19:35.470 --> 00:19:39.010
Goodbye, Emily, my love.

00:19:39.070 --> 00:19:44.022
Goodbye, Palamon, my brother.

00:19:44.082 --> 00:19:49.136
And then, our sight died.

00:19:49.196 --> 00:19:57.380
Soon it was winter, and the king called for Palamon and Emily.

00:19:57.440 --> 00:20:06.633
As you know, our sight died last summer, and it was very sad, said the king.

00:20:06.693 --> 00:20:10.964
Emily, I want you to be happy.

00:20:11.024 --> 00:20:14.595
Palamon, you must marry Emily.

00:20:14.655 --> 00:20:17.858
It's the right thing to do.

00:20:17.918 --> 00:20:21.702
Thank you, said Palamon.

00:20:21.762 --> 00:20:24.474
Our sight was a good night.

00:20:24.534 --> 00:20:27.286
He was my dear brother.

00:20:27.346 --> 00:20:31.540
But we had to fight for love.

00:20:31.600 --> 00:20:36.444
Emily, I know we'll be happy together.

00:20:36.504 --> 00:20:40.346
But we'll never forget my brother.

00:20:40.406 --> 00:20:46.286
He died for love.

00:20:46.346 --> 00:20:56.974
The Clark's Tale The Clark was the next person to tell his story.

00:20:57.034 --> 00:21:01.274
I have an interesting story, he said.

00:21:01.334 --> 00:21:04.415
It's about a king called Walter.

00:21:04.475 --> 00:21:08.556
He was the king of Saluche in Italy.

00:21:08.616 --> 00:21:15.968
Walter wanted to marry a woman, but only he knew the name of this woman.

00:21:16.028 --> 00:21:18.678
It was his secret.

00:21:18.738 --> 00:21:22.468
The woman's name was Griselda.

00:21:22.528 --> 00:21:27.390
She was young and beautiful, and she was very nice.

00:21:27.450 --> 00:21:33.462
She was very poor, and she lived in a small house with her father.

00:21:33.522 --> 00:21:37.452
She cooked and cleaned for him every day.

00:21:37.512 --> 00:21:45.225
And now, I'll tell you their story, said the clerk.

00:21:45.285 --> 00:21:51.959
One day, Griselda was at home with her father.

00:21:52.019 --> 00:21:56.442
Today is the day, said Griselda.

00:21:56.502 --> 00:22:00.686
Today we'll know the name of the king's wife.

00:22:00.746 --> 00:22:02.217
Who will it be?

00:22:02.237 --> 00:22:06.081
It's very exciting.

00:22:06.141 --> 00:22:12.766
I think his wife will be a rich woman, said Griselda's father.

00:22:12.827 --> 00:22:16.697
But Griselda's father was wrong.

00:22:16.757 --> 00:22:20.658
and soon he heard somebody at the door.

00:22:20.718 --> 00:22:29.476
Grisalda's father opened the door, and he saw Walter, the King of Saldre.

00:22:29.536 --> 00:22:32.608
I want to speak to you.

00:22:32.668 --> 00:22:37.372
I want to marry Grisalda, said Walter.

00:22:37.432 --> 00:22:44.909
Grisalda, my Grisalda, said the father.

00:22:44.969 --> 00:22:51.662
If this is strange, we are poor, and you're the king.

00:22:51.722 --> 00:22:55.244
Why do you want a poor wife?"

00:22:55.304 --> 00:22:59.296
That's not important, said Walter.

00:22:59.356 --> 00:23:02.148
She's the woman I love.

00:23:02.208 --> 00:23:05.038
Can I speak to her?

00:23:05.098 --> 00:23:10.382
Well, of course, said the father.

00:23:10.442 --> 00:23:14.697
And then Walter went inside the house.

00:23:14.757 --> 00:23:17.662
and he spoke to Griselda.

00:23:17.722 --> 00:23:23.236
Griselda, said Walter, will you be my wife?

00:23:23.296 --> 00:23:27.060
You must do everything I say.

00:23:27.120 --> 00:23:31.634
I'm too poor for you, said Griselda.

00:23:31.694 --> 00:23:34.115
I cook and clean.

00:23:34.175 --> 00:23:36.096
I work hard.

00:23:36.156 --> 00:23:39.660
I have a different kind of life.

00:23:39.720 --> 00:23:43.510
But I want you to be happy.

00:23:43.570 --> 00:23:50.212
I'll be your wife, and I promise to do everything you say."

00:23:50.272 --> 00:23:54.524
That's good, said Walter.

00:23:54.584 --> 00:23:58.837
And then Griselda went home with Walter.

00:23:58.898 --> 00:24:01.230
Servants arrived.

00:24:01.290 --> 00:24:10.260
They gave Griselda a beautiful dress, and on that day Walter married Griselda.

00:24:10.320 --> 00:24:14.816
Walter and Griselda were very happy.

00:24:14.876 --> 00:24:18.067
The people of the city liked her.

00:24:18.128 --> 00:24:22.900
Soon, Griselda had a beautiful baby girl.

00:24:22.960 --> 00:24:26.012
Walter was also happy.

00:24:26.072 --> 00:24:29.604
But he was worried about something.

00:24:29.664 --> 00:24:34.186
Griselda is very nice, he thought.

00:24:34.246 --> 00:24:37.808
But does she love me?

00:24:37.868 --> 00:24:42.042
Is she only nice because I'm the king?

00:24:42.102 --> 00:24:46.494
I have to know that she loves me.

00:24:46.554 --> 00:24:52.476
Then, Walter did something very bad.

00:24:52.537 --> 00:24:56.989
One night, Griselda was in her room.

00:24:57.049 --> 00:24:59.310
She was with her daughter.

00:24:59.370 --> 00:25:03.012
Walter's servant came into the room.

00:25:03.072 --> 00:25:09.424
I'm sorry it's late, said the servant, but I must do what the king says.

00:25:09.444 --> 00:25:13.281
I must take your daughter.

00:25:13.341 --> 00:25:17.629
The servant took the child from Griselda.

00:25:17.689 --> 00:25:20.531
Griselda was very worried.

00:25:20.591 --> 00:25:23.613
What's he going to do with my daughter?

00:25:23.673 --> 00:25:25.644
Is he going to kill her?

00:25:25.704 --> 00:25:27.706
Thought Griselda.

00:25:27.766 --> 00:25:31.228
But Griselda said nothing.

00:25:31.288 --> 00:25:39.783
Now go, said Griselda to the servant, and do what the king says.

00:25:39.843 --> 00:25:44.775
Then the servant took the child to Walter.

00:25:44.835 --> 00:25:50.536
Don't tell anybody about this," said Walter to his servant.

00:25:50.596 --> 00:25:54.066
Go with my daughter to Milan.

00:25:54.126 --> 00:25:56.747
She'll live with my sister.

00:25:56.807 --> 00:26:00.378
But remember, it's a secret.

00:26:00.438 --> 00:26:05.059
Nobody must know that this girl is my daughter.

00:26:05.120 --> 00:26:10.661
And then the king's servant took the child to Milan.

00:26:10.721 --> 00:26:14.066
What did Griselda do?

00:26:14.126 --> 00:26:17.240
Did she hate her husband?

00:26:17.300 --> 00:26:21.751
The answer to this question is no.

00:26:21.811 --> 00:26:25.362
Griselda didn't change.

00:26:25.422 --> 00:26:30.573
Does Griselda love me or not thought the king?

00:26:30.593 --> 00:26:36.144
Oh, I don't know.

00:26:36.204 --> 00:26:42.516
After five years, Griselda had another baby.

00:26:42.576 --> 00:26:44.705
It was a boy.

00:26:44.765 --> 00:26:48.316
Griselda was happy again.

00:26:48.376 --> 00:26:51.718
But Walter wasn't happy.

00:26:51.778 --> 00:26:58.802
Griselda, said Walter, do you promise that you'll always love me?

00:26:58.862 --> 00:27:02.976
Yes, I do, said Griselda.

00:27:03.036 --> 00:27:07.798
I'm your wife, and I left my old life.

00:27:07.858 --> 00:27:11.140
I left my house and my father.

00:27:11.200 --> 00:27:13.502
I'll die for you.

00:27:13.562 --> 00:27:16.082
Is that what you want?

00:27:16.143 --> 00:27:19.433
but Walter wasn't happy.

00:27:19.493 --> 00:27:25.256
I have to know that she loves me, he thought.

00:27:25.316 --> 00:27:30.448
Soon, Griselda's son was two years old.

00:27:30.508 --> 00:27:34.410
One night, Griselda was in her room.

00:27:34.470 --> 00:27:36.860
She was with her son.

00:27:36.920 --> 00:27:41.652
Then, the servant came into her room again.

00:27:41.712 --> 00:27:45.854
I must take your son," he said.

00:27:45.914 --> 00:27:48.897
It's what the king wants.

00:27:48.957 --> 00:27:56.122
First my daughter and now my son thought Griselda.

00:27:56.182 --> 00:28:02.997
Oh my children, what will Walter do to my son?

00:28:03.057 --> 00:28:11.935
Griselda said goodbye to her son, and then the servant took the child to Walter.

00:28:11.995 --> 00:28:17.098
Take my son to Bologna, said Walter.

00:28:17.158 --> 00:28:21.880
And remember, this must be a secret.

00:28:21.941 --> 00:28:25.062
And then the servant left.

00:28:25.122 --> 00:28:29.644
He took the boy to a family in Bologna.

00:28:29.704 --> 00:28:34.115
Now I'll know, thought the king.

00:28:34.175 --> 00:28:38.176
Will Griselda love me now?

00:28:38.236 --> 00:28:41.690
But Griselda didn't change.

00:28:41.750 --> 00:28:46.106
She didn't hate Walter, she was good to him.

00:28:46.166 --> 00:28:51.612
I don't know what Walter is thinking, thought Griselda.

00:28:51.672 --> 00:28:56.566
I promised to love him, and I will love him.

00:28:56.626 --> 00:29:01.521
But why does he do these bad things?

00:29:01.582 --> 00:29:06.316
For some years, Walter was happy.

00:29:06.376 --> 00:29:12.792
His daughter was in Milan, and she was now 18 years old.

00:29:12.852 --> 00:29:16.835
And Walter began to worry again.

00:29:16.895 --> 00:29:20.188
Does Griselda love me?

00:29:20.248 --> 00:29:22.500
He thought again.

00:29:22.560 --> 00:29:26.562
And then he did another bad thing.

00:29:26.622 --> 00:29:34.258
The king called for Griselda, and he said to her, I don't need you anymore.

00:29:34.318 --> 00:29:36.690
I want a new wife.

00:29:36.750 --> 00:29:39.631
Griselda said nothing.

00:29:39.691 --> 00:29:43.553
And then she left Walter's room.

00:29:43.613 --> 00:29:47.766
Walter then spoke to his servant.

00:29:47.826 --> 00:29:51.427
Bring me my son and daughter, he said.

00:29:51.487 --> 00:29:53.668
But it must be a secret.

00:29:53.728 --> 00:29:57.320
Don't tell anybody who these children are.

00:29:57.380 --> 00:30:01.082
I'll say to everybody that I'm going to marry the girl.

00:30:01.142 --> 00:30:03.503
Of course I'm not going to marry her.

00:30:03.563 --> 00:30:04.864
She's my daughter.

00:30:04.924 --> 00:30:08.278
But nobody will know this.

00:30:08.338 --> 00:30:14.354
That afternoon, Walter spoke to Griselda again.

00:30:14.414 --> 00:30:19.736
Griselda, a poor woman can't be my wife.

00:30:19.797 --> 00:30:22.718
I was wrong, he said.

00:30:22.779 --> 00:30:25.490
My new wife is arriving.

00:30:25.550 --> 00:30:28.511
You must go back to your father's home.

00:30:28.572 --> 00:30:30.492
Leave your clothes here.

00:30:30.552 --> 00:30:34.214
I'll give them to my new wife.

00:30:34.274 --> 00:30:39.066
Thank you for everything, said Griselda.

00:30:39.126 --> 00:30:42.028
I'll go home to my father.

00:30:42.088 --> 00:30:44.179
He's old.

00:30:44.239 --> 00:30:48.603
I want you to be happy with your new wife."

00:30:48.663 --> 00:30:52.526
And then she left the room.

00:30:52.586 --> 00:30:56.530
The king was very sad.

00:30:56.590 --> 00:31:00.164
I hate doing this, he thought.

00:31:00.224 --> 00:31:07.327
I love her so much, but I must know that she loves me.

00:31:07.387 --> 00:31:12.808
The next day, Walter went to Griselda's house.

00:31:12.868 --> 00:31:16.762
He wanted to ask Griselda something.

00:31:16.822 --> 00:31:23.807
Griselda, as you know, my new wife is arriving, said Walter.

00:31:23.867 --> 00:31:27.240
I need somebody to clean her room.

00:31:27.300 --> 00:31:29.682
Will you help me?

00:31:29.742 --> 00:31:34.366
I'll be happy to help, said Griselda.

00:31:34.426 --> 00:31:37.670
And then she went to Walter's house.

00:31:37.731 --> 00:31:44.176
She cleaned the rooms, she made the beds, and she washed the plates.

00:31:44.236 --> 00:31:49.968
That morning, Griselda's son and daughter arrived.

00:31:50.028 --> 00:31:59.251
When Griselda saw the girl, she thought, she's beautiful, and she thought of her daughter.

00:31:59.312 --> 00:32:03.488
My daughter is the same age, she thought.

00:32:03.548 --> 00:32:07.935
And when Griselda saw the boy, she thought of her son.

00:32:07.955 --> 00:32:11.927
The boy is so clever.

00:32:11.987 --> 00:32:15.508
My son is the same age.

00:32:15.568 --> 00:32:20.922
Of course, she didn't know that they were her children.

00:32:20.981 --> 00:32:27.745
When Griselda saw the king, she said, That girl is very nice.

00:32:27.805 --> 00:32:29.536
She's beautiful.

00:32:29.596 --> 00:32:31.937
Be nice to her.

00:32:31.997 --> 00:32:34.757
I hope you'll be happy.

00:32:34.817 --> 00:32:38.468
Stop this," said the king.

00:32:38.529 --> 00:32:41.420
I don't want to do this anymore.

00:32:41.480 --> 00:32:47.035
My dear wife, Griselda, I love you very much.

00:32:47.095 --> 00:32:53.500
Griselda, you are my wife and you're perfect.

00:32:53.560 --> 00:32:58.824
And then Walter called for his son and daughter.

00:32:58.884 --> 00:33:05.706
Griselda, this is our daughter and not my new wife.

00:33:05.766 --> 00:33:09.015
And this is our son.

00:33:09.075 --> 00:33:11.646
I'm very sorry.

00:33:11.706 --> 00:33:14.707
I only wanted you to love me.

00:33:14.767 --> 00:33:18.218
And now I know that you do.

00:33:18.278 --> 00:33:22.440
These are our children.

00:33:22.500 --> 00:33:27.561
Griselda was happy to see her children again.

00:33:27.621 --> 00:33:29.072
Thank you.

00:33:29.132 --> 00:33:31.552
Thank you, said Griselda.

00:33:31.612 --> 00:33:34.866
My children are safe.

00:33:34.926 --> 00:33:39.160
That night they had a big party.

00:33:39.220 --> 00:33:43.954
Griselda and Walter were both very happy.

00:33:44.014 --> 00:33:50.839
And Walter never worried about Griselda's love again.

00:33:50.900 --> 00:34:01.148
Chapter 4 The Merchant's Tale The merchant told the next story.

00:34:01.208 --> 00:34:04.508
I travel a lot, he said.

00:34:04.568 --> 00:34:09.518
And everywhere I go, I see people that are sad.

00:34:09.578 --> 00:34:11.758
I have a wife.

00:34:11.818 --> 00:34:14.189
But do you think I'm happy?

00:34:14.249 --> 00:34:17.460
Well, I'm not happy.

00:34:17.519 --> 00:34:20.590
My wife isn't a nice person.

00:34:20.650 --> 00:34:23.451
And I hate my life.

00:34:23.511 --> 00:34:28.252
I want to tell you a story about her husband and wife.

00:34:28.312 --> 00:34:32.192
It's a story about a rich old man.

00:34:32.252 --> 00:34:35.331
His name is January.

00:34:35.392 --> 00:34:41.911
January wanted to find a wife, and he asked his friends to help him.

00:34:41.971 --> 00:34:46.382
Don't find me an old wife, said January.

00:34:46.442 --> 00:34:49.102
I want a young wife.

00:34:49.163 --> 00:34:52.893
January's friends found a wife for him.

00:34:52.953 --> 00:34:55.164
Her name was May.

00:34:55.224 --> 00:34:59.824
She was young, but she didn't have any money.

00:34:59.884 --> 00:35:03.640
January was happy with his wife.

00:35:03.701 --> 00:35:06.267
I'm old, he thought.

00:35:06.327 --> 00:35:09.168
But now I've got a young wife.

00:35:09.228 --> 00:35:11.929
I won't have any more problems.

00:35:11.989 --> 00:35:15.970
And May is very beautiful.

00:35:16.031 --> 00:35:21.783
But there was another person who thought that May was beautiful.

00:35:21.843 --> 00:35:24.674
It was January 7th.

00:35:24.734 --> 00:35:27.496
His name was Damien.

00:35:27.556 --> 00:35:31.684
Damien thought of May all the time.

00:35:31.744 --> 00:35:34.012
He didn't sleep very much.

00:35:34.072 --> 00:35:35.953
He didn't want to eat.

00:35:36.013 --> 00:35:38.274
He loved May.

00:35:38.334 --> 00:35:44.267
And now he had to see her every day with January.

00:35:44.327 --> 00:35:47.448
Soon Damien wasn't well.

00:35:47.508 --> 00:35:50.220
He didn't want to go to work anymore.

00:35:50.280 --> 00:35:52.532
And he stayed in bed.

00:35:52.592 --> 00:35:56.503
In bed, he wrote a letter to May.

00:35:56.563 --> 00:36:00.920
Then he put the letter in a small bag.

00:36:00.980 --> 00:36:04.948
That evening, January went to dinner.

00:36:05.008 --> 00:36:07.590
Where's my servant Damien?

00:36:07.650 --> 00:36:08.942
He said.

00:36:09.002 --> 00:36:13.004
Damien isn't well, said another servant.

00:36:13.064 --> 00:36:15.546
He's in bed now.

00:36:15.606 --> 00:36:19.278
I'm sorry about that, said January.

00:36:19.339 --> 00:36:21.310
He's a good servant.

00:36:21.370 --> 00:36:23.362
He works hard.

00:36:23.422 --> 00:36:26.484
I want to speak to him.

00:36:26.544 --> 00:36:31.790
After dinner, May and January visited Damien.

00:36:31.850 --> 00:36:35.075
May went to see Damien first.

00:36:35.135 --> 00:36:37.596
She sat next to him.

00:36:37.656 --> 00:36:39.487
How are you?

00:36:39.547 --> 00:36:41.328
asked May.

00:36:41.388 --> 00:36:44.750
Damien didn't say anything.

00:36:44.810 --> 00:36:51.452
He took the letter out of his bag, and then he gave the letter to May.

00:36:51.513 --> 00:36:56.964
Don't speak to anybody about this letter, he said.

00:36:57.024 --> 00:37:02.605
When May was at home, she read Damien's letter.

00:37:02.665 --> 00:37:05.354
It was a love letter.

00:37:05.414 --> 00:37:08.546
May didn't know what to do.

00:37:08.607 --> 00:37:13.140
Damien doesn't know my secret, she thought.

00:37:13.200 --> 00:37:20.154
I love Damien, but he is poor, and my husband is rich.

00:37:20.214 --> 00:37:23.085
How can I help Damien?

00:37:23.146 --> 00:37:27.818
I want him to be well again, thought May.

00:37:27.879 --> 00:37:31.369
May wrote a letter to Damien.

00:37:31.429 --> 00:37:34.609
And then she visited him again.

00:37:34.669 --> 00:37:37.932
She gave Damien the letter.

00:37:37.992 --> 00:37:41.904
Get well soon Damien, she said.

00:37:41.964 --> 00:37:44.866
And then she left.

00:37:44.926 --> 00:37:48.198
Damien read the letter.

00:37:48.259 --> 00:37:51.140
The letter changed him.

00:37:51.201 --> 00:37:54.012
Soon he was well again.

00:37:54.072 --> 00:37:57.864
The next morning Damien got up.

00:37:57.924 --> 00:38:00.333
Now he was happy.

00:38:00.394 --> 00:38:03.874
Now he wanted to go to work.

00:38:03.934 --> 00:38:09.896
January had a big house and he had a beautiful garden.

00:38:09.956 --> 00:38:12.337
He often went there.

00:38:12.397 --> 00:38:15.468
It was his favorite place.

00:38:15.528 --> 00:38:19.999
Only January and May could go to the garden.

00:38:20.059 --> 00:38:26.924
January had a key and he used the key to go into the garden.

00:38:26.984 --> 00:38:31.560
One day, January was in his garden.

00:38:31.620 --> 00:38:34.821
He looked at the trees and the flowers.

00:38:34.881 --> 00:38:37.372
It was a beautiful day.

00:38:37.432 --> 00:38:39.903
The weather was perfect.

00:38:39.963 --> 00:38:43.194
But January didn't feel very well.

00:38:43.254 --> 00:38:44.395
Help!

00:38:44.455 --> 00:38:45.375
Help!

00:38:45.436 --> 00:38:46.776
Said January.

00:38:46.836 --> 00:38:48.097
I can't see!

00:38:48.117 --> 00:38:51.008
I can't see anything!

00:38:51.068 --> 00:38:53.149
I'm blind!

00:38:53.209 --> 00:38:55.992
It was very sad.

00:38:56.053 --> 00:38:59.846
January couldn't see any more.

00:38:59.906 --> 00:39:05.970
May went to the garden, and she took January back to the house.

00:39:06.031 --> 00:39:10.534
January stayed in his room for two months.

00:39:10.594 --> 00:39:15.346
He didn't want to go out, and he often thought about May.

00:39:15.406 --> 00:39:17.628
What about May?

00:39:17.688 --> 00:39:18.968
He thought.

00:39:19.029 --> 00:39:22.730
Now I can't see my beautiful wife.

00:39:22.790 --> 00:39:24.852
What is he doing?

00:39:24.912 --> 00:39:28.023
I can't see what she's doing.

00:39:28.083 --> 00:39:30.534
Does she love me?

00:39:30.594 --> 00:39:33.345
I know what I'll do.

00:39:33.405 --> 00:39:38.047
I'll tell her that she must always stay in the house.

00:39:38.107 --> 00:39:41.478
We'll stay here together.

00:39:41.538 --> 00:39:48.851
The next day, January said to May, you must always sit next to me.

00:39:48.911 --> 00:39:51.592
Then I'll know what you're doing.

00:39:51.652 --> 00:39:54.722
Sometimes we can go to the garden.

00:39:54.782 --> 00:39:58.202
but we must go there together.

00:39:58.262 --> 00:40:02.205
Now it was May who was sad.

00:40:02.265 --> 00:40:04.857
Her house was a prison.

00:40:04.917 --> 00:40:09.280
And she thought more and more about Damien.

00:40:09.341 --> 00:40:12.402
Damien was also sad.

00:40:12.462 --> 00:40:16.025
I can't speak to May, he thought.

00:40:16.085 --> 00:40:18.687
January is always there.

00:40:18.747 --> 00:40:20.598
I must do something.

00:40:20.658 --> 00:40:23.082
I need to speak to May.

00:40:23.142 --> 00:40:27.536
May and Damien often wrote letters to each other.

00:40:27.596 --> 00:40:30.108
They wrote about their love.

00:40:30.168 --> 00:40:32.781
But Damien wanted more.

00:40:32.841 --> 00:40:35.894
He wanted to speak to May.

00:40:35.954 --> 00:40:38.726
He wrote a letter to her.

00:40:38.786 --> 00:40:48.354
In the letter he wrote, May, take a key to the garden and then give the key to me.

00:40:48.414 --> 00:40:51.390
January has a lot of keys.

00:40:51.450 --> 00:40:56.074
Then tell January that you want to go to the garden.

00:40:56.134 --> 00:40:58.556
Do it now.

00:40:58.616 --> 00:41:04.509
Damien gave the letter to May and May did what Damien asked.

00:41:04.569 --> 00:41:06.930
She gave him the key.

00:41:06.991 --> 00:41:14.494
Then Damien went to the garden and he waited there for January and May.

00:41:14.554 --> 00:41:19.036
Soon January and May were in the garden.

00:41:19.096 --> 00:41:22.116
January was happy again.

00:41:22.176 --> 00:41:27.298
I'm old, and I can't see," he said to May.

00:41:27.358 --> 00:41:30.291
But I have you, my love.

00:41:30.351 --> 00:41:36.596
I love you so much, and I want to show you how much I love you.

00:41:36.656 --> 00:41:44.192
Tomorrow I'm going to give you all my money and this house and this gun.

00:41:44.252 --> 00:41:47.635
January, what are you saying?

00:41:47.695 --> 00:41:48.926
Said May.

00:41:48.986 --> 00:41:52.119
You're the only man in my life.

00:41:52.179 --> 00:41:59.563
But of course, there was another man in May's life, and that man was Damien.

00:41:59.623 --> 00:42:04.456
And now she saw Damien in the garden.

00:42:04.516 --> 00:42:08.266
I'm hungry, said May.

00:42:08.326 --> 00:42:10.838
I want to go to the apple tree.

00:42:10.898 --> 00:42:12.949
Then I can eat an apple.

00:42:13.009 --> 00:42:14.640
Wait here.

00:42:14.700 --> 00:42:17.751
But May didn't want any apples.

00:42:17.811 --> 00:42:20.232
She didn't go to the tree.

00:42:20.292 --> 00:42:23.816
She ran to meet Damien.

00:42:23.876 --> 00:42:27.301
January waited for May.

00:42:27.361 --> 00:42:29.984
He didn't know where she was.

00:42:30.044 --> 00:42:33.516
Now she was with Damien.

00:42:33.576 --> 00:42:38.310
But then everything changed.

00:42:38.370 --> 00:42:41.343
I can see again.

00:42:41.403 --> 00:42:45.586
I can see, said January to himself.

00:42:45.647 --> 00:42:47.838
How is this possible?

00:42:47.898 --> 00:42:49.460
He thought.

00:42:49.520 --> 00:42:52.554
January didn't understand.

00:42:52.614 --> 00:42:56.810
I must tell May, she'll be so happy."

00:42:56.870 --> 00:43:03.604
And so January looked at the apple tree, but May wasn't there.

00:43:03.665 --> 00:43:07.668
Where's May thought January?

00:43:07.728 --> 00:43:13.832
And then he saw her, but he didn't only see May.

00:43:13.893 --> 00:43:17.044
He also saw a man.

00:43:17.105 --> 00:43:19.076
Who are you?

00:43:19.136 --> 00:43:20.956
What are you doing?

00:43:21.016 --> 00:43:25.776
Leave this garden now, said January.

00:43:25.836 --> 00:43:30.358
Damien and May looked at January.

00:43:30.418 --> 00:43:37.420
I think he can see us, said Damien, and then Damien ran.

00:43:37.480 --> 00:43:42.872
He was very fast, and soon he was outside the garden.

00:43:42.933 --> 00:43:47.294
Then May ran to speak to January.

00:43:47.355 --> 00:43:49.626
What is it, my love?

00:43:49.686 --> 00:43:51.625
She asked.

00:43:51.685 --> 00:43:54.424
I can see now.

00:43:54.484 --> 00:43:56.325
I was so happy.

00:43:56.385 --> 00:43:58.346
I wanted to tell you.

00:43:58.406 --> 00:44:01.846
And then I saw you with a man.

00:44:01.906 --> 00:44:05.678
I think I saw you with somebody."

00:44:05.738 --> 00:44:08.338
You can see again?

00:44:08.399 --> 00:44:09.749
said May.

00:44:09.809 --> 00:44:12.030
I'm so happy.

00:44:12.090 --> 00:44:15.881
But what are you talking about?

00:44:15.941 --> 00:44:17.532
A man?

00:44:17.592 --> 00:44:26.535
You can look everywhere in this garden, but you won't see a man, because there is no man."

00:44:26.595 --> 00:44:32.647
I was so excited that I could see again, said January.

00:44:32.707 --> 00:44:40.170
I think I saw something that wasn't there, but I thought there was somebody with you.

00:44:40.230 --> 00:44:43.741
There was no man, said May.

00:44:43.801 --> 00:44:46.908
Nobody can come into the garden.

00:44:46.968 --> 00:44:49.774
I want to go back home, my love.

00:44:49.834 --> 00:44:52.144
Then you can sleep.

00:44:52.204 --> 00:44:54.144
You're tired."

00:44:54.204 --> 00:44:55.655
Yes.

00:44:55.715 --> 00:44:58.796
You're right, said January.

00:44:58.856 --> 00:45:02.276
Of course there wasn't a man.

00:45:02.337 --> 00:45:05.688
Nobody can come into the garden.

00:45:05.748 --> 00:45:08.398
I want to go home now.

00:45:08.458 --> 00:45:12.739
We have to tell everybody, we'll have a party.

00:45:12.799 --> 00:45:14.530
Isn't it great?

00:45:14.590 --> 00:45:16.892
I'm not blind.

00:45:16.952 --> 00:45:20.176
I can see again."

00:45:20.236 --> 00:45:25.620
And here my story ends, said the merchant.

00:45:25.680 --> 00:45:27.832
January was happy.

00:45:27.892 --> 00:45:30.074
He could see again.

00:45:30.134 --> 00:45:34.228
But there was something that January couldn't see.

00:45:34.288 --> 00:45:38.212
He couldn't see that May didn't love him.

00:45:38.272 --> 00:45:41.804
And that May loved Damien.

00:45:41.864 --> 00:45:45.715
January wasn't blind anymore.

00:45:45.775 --> 00:45:51.496
But love is always blind.

00:45:51.556 --> 00:46:02.582
Chapter 5 The Franklin's Tale Everybody in the group was tired.

00:46:02.642 --> 00:46:05.574
It was the end of a long day.

00:46:05.634 --> 00:46:10.336
They were ready to listen to the Franklin story.

00:46:10.397 --> 00:46:15.520
My story is also about a husband and wife.

00:46:15.580 --> 00:46:20.474
But this story is different from the merchant story.

00:46:20.534 --> 00:46:24.798
In my story, love is not blind.

00:46:24.858 --> 00:46:28.780
The husband and wife in my story are in love.

00:46:28.840 --> 00:46:32.224
The wife's name was Dorigen.

00:46:32.284 --> 00:46:35.606
She loved her husband very much.

00:46:35.667 --> 00:46:39.450
The husband's name was Arviragos.

00:46:39.510 --> 00:46:41.572
He was a knight.

00:46:41.632 --> 00:46:43.979
They lived in France.

00:46:44.039 --> 00:46:49.158
But when I start my story, Arvidagus was in England.

00:46:49.218 --> 00:46:51.929
Dorogen was very sad.

00:46:51.989 --> 00:46:59.924
She thought about her husband every day, and she stayed at home.

00:46:59.984 --> 00:47:05.086
Arvidagus wrote a letter to Dorogen.

00:47:05.147 --> 00:47:10.010
Don't worry, I'll come home soon, he wrote.

00:47:10.070 --> 00:47:13.046
Dorogen read the letter.

00:47:13.106 --> 00:47:15.533
I don't want him to come back soon.

00:47:15.553 --> 00:47:18.916
I wanted to come back now," she thought.

00:47:18.976 --> 00:47:21.166
But I must go out.

00:47:21.226 --> 00:47:24.568
I must try to be happy.

00:47:24.629 --> 00:47:28.911
And so Dorogen started going out.

00:47:28.972 --> 00:47:31.744
Her house was near the sea.

00:47:31.804 --> 00:47:39.698
She often went for a walk there with her friends, and she always wanted to look at the sea.

00:47:39.758 --> 00:47:46.330
Where is the boat thought, Dorogen, that will bring me my husband?

00:47:46.390 --> 00:47:51.772
And sometimes she looked at the big black rocks in the sea.

00:47:51.832 --> 00:47:56.523
I don't like the sea, said Dorogen to her friends.

00:47:56.583 --> 00:47:59.184
Look at those black rocks.

00:47:59.244 --> 00:48:01.785
They're dangerous.

00:48:01.845 --> 00:48:05.670
Dorogen's friends were very worried.

00:48:05.730 --> 00:48:11.534
You must stop thinking about those dangerous black rocks, they said.

00:48:11.594 --> 00:48:16.416
And so Dorogen's friends took her to a dance.

00:48:16.476 --> 00:48:20.147
But she didn't want to dance.

00:48:20.207 --> 00:48:25.098
At the dance there was a man called Aurelius.

00:48:25.158 --> 00:48:31.312
He loved Dorogen, and he wanted to speak to her.

00:48:31.372 --> 00:48:35.776
Dorogen, you don't know me very well.

00:48:35.836 --> 00:48:38.527
My name is Aurelius.

00:48:38.588 --> 00:48:41.500
You're so beautiful.

00:48:41.560 --> 00:48:45.702
Is there a place in your heart for me?

00:48:45.763 --> 00:48:51.186
Dorogen looked at Aurelius and said, No, there isn't.

00:48:51.246 --> 00:48:54.858
I'll always love my husband.

00:48:54.918 --> 00:48:57.229
But what will I do?

00:48:57.249 --> 00:49:00.696
I need you, said Aurelius.

00:49:00.756 --> 00:49:04.434
I'm sorry," said Dorogen.

00:49:04.495 --> 00:49:09.849
But, said Aurelius, is there anything I can do?

00:49:09.869 --> 00:49:17.916
Hmm, well, I want the black rocks in the sea to disappear.

00:49:17.976 --> 00:49:23.370
Do this, and then there will be a place in my heart for you.

00:49:23.431 --> 00:49:27.044
But that's not possible, said Aurelius.

00:49:27.104 --> 00:49:29.370
Nobody can do this.

00:49:29.430 --> 00:49:32.945
I know, said Dorogen.

00:49:33.005 --> 00:49:35.986
Aurelius went home.

00:49:36.046 --> 00:49:38.976
At home he said a prayer.

00:49:39.036 --> 00:49:41.848
Help me, he said.

00:49:41.908 --> 00:49:44.788
And then he went to bed.

00:49:44.848 --> 00:49:47.379
And he stayed at home.

00:49:47.439 --> 00:49:49.540
He never went out.

00:49:49.600 --> 00:49:53.451
He didn't want to see anybody.

00:49:53.511 --> 00:49:57.748
Soon Dorogen's husband came home.

00:49:57.808 --> 00:50:01.256
Dorogen and Arviragus were together again.

00:50:01.276 --> 00:50:04.576
Aurelius was at home.

00:50:04.636 --> 00:50:08.497
He was always at home.

00:50:08.557 --> 00:50:14.038
One day Aurelius read an interesting book.

00:50:14.098 --> 00:50:17.348
It was a book about magic.

00:50:17.408 --> 00:50:20.379
I can use magic.

00:50:20.439 --> 00:50:26.162
With magic, the black rocks will disappear, thought Aurelius.

00:50:26.222 --> 00:50:29.175
I know a man in Orleans.

00:50:29.235 --> 00:50:31.095
His name is Simon.

00:50:31.155 --> 00:50:33.756
He is famous for his magic.

00:50:33.816 --> 00:50:36.957
I can ask him to help me.

00:50:37.017 --> 00:50:42.519
The next day Aurelius went to Simon's house.

00:50:42.579 --> 00:50:45.400
Hello, said Simon.

00:50:45.460 --> 00:50:49.535
Have dinner with me and you can tell me everything.

00:50:49.595 --> 00:50:53.762
At dinner there was every kind of food.

00:50:53.822 --> 00:50:58.136
There was meat, fish, fruit and vegetables.

00:50:58.196 --> 00:51:03.840
They ate and Aurelius told Simon his story.

00:51:03.900 --> 00:51:07.544
Simon listened to the story.

00:51:07.604 --> 00:51:13.208
And then he said, It's true that I sometimes do magic.

00:51:13.268 --> 00:51:17.385
And now I'll do some magic for you.

00:51:17.445 --> 00:51:23.140
And then the food on the table disappeared.

00:51:23.201 --> 00:51:26.701
Aurelius was very happy.

00:51:26.762 --> 00:51:32.343
Can you help me, said Aurelius, with the black rocks?

00:51:32.403 --> 00:51:38.565
Yes, I can, said Simon, but it'll be expensive.

00:51:38.625 --> 00:51:41.876
You have to pay me a thousand pounds.

00:51:41.936 --> 00:51:45.865
That's a lot of money, said Aurelius.

00:51:45.925 --> 00:51:49.254
But all right, you must be quick.

00:51:49.314 --> 00:51:52.406
I want to go home tomorrow."

00:51:52.466 --> 00:51:57.057
In the morning they went back to Aurelius' house.

00:51:57.117 --> 00:52:02.699
Simon started work, and after two days he was ready.

00:52:02.759 --> 00:52:08.471
Aurelius, he said, we can go and see the black rocks.

00:52:08.531 --> 00:52:10.752
They went to the sea.

00:52:10.812 --> 00:52:16.740
But when they arrived, the black rocks weren't there anymore.

00:52:16.801 --> 00:52:18.838
Oh, thank you.

00:52:18.898 --> 00:52:21.920
Thank you so much, Sir Aurelius.

00:52:21.980 --> 00:52:25.152
I must show this to Dorogen.

00:52:25.212 --> 00:52:30.184
The next day, Aurelius met Dorogen.

00:52:30.245 --> 00:52:33.416
Hello, Dorogen, he said.

00:52:33.476 --> 00:52:38.200
Do you remember our conversation about the dangerous black rocks?

00:52:38.260 --> 00:52:41.181
Do you remember what you promised?

00:52:41.242 --> 00:52:44.547
Please tell me that you remember.

00:52:44.607 --> 00:52:49.244
Yes, I remember, said Dorogen.

00:52:49.304 --> 00:52:56.830
Well, said Aurelius, the black rocks aren't there anymore, come and see.

00:52:56.890 --> 00:53:01.683
When they arrived, Dorogen looked at the sea.

00:53:01.743 --> 00:53:08.818
And then she said, but how can black rocks disappear?

00:53:08.878 --> 00:53:11.089
What can I do?

00:53:11.150 --> 00:53:14.234
I have to speak to my husband.

00:53:14.294 --> 00:53:18.108
And then she ran back home.

00:53:18.168 --> 00:53:26.214
When Dorogen arrived home, she started to think, I need a promise.

00:53:26.274 --> 00:53:28.976
And promises are important.

00:53:29.036 --> 00:53:32.658
But I'll never do anything bad to my husband.

00:53:32.718 --> 00:53:35.060
What can I do?

00:53:35.120 --> 00:53:40.074
For two days, Dorogen thought about her problem.

00:53:40.134 --> 00:53:47.976
What can I say to my husband, she thought, Then Dorogen spoke to her husband.

00:53:48.036 --> 00:53:51.248
She told him everything.

00:53:51.308 --> 00:53:54.840
Don't worry, said Aviragus.

00:53:54.900 --> 00:53:57.132
You did nothing wrong.

00:53:57.192 --> 00:54:01.476
But you promised this to Aurelius.

00:54:01.536 --> 00:54:05.068
And that's why you must leave me.

00:54:05.128 --> 00:54:09.692
But I love you, Aviragus, said Dorogen.

00:54:09.752 --> 00:54:12.756
Oh, what can I do?

00:54:12.816 --> 00:54:15.621
Dorogen went to a garden.

00:54:15.682 --> 00:54:17.614
She needed to think.

00:54:17.674 --> 00:54:22.818
When she was in the garden, a man spoke to her.

00:54:22.878 --> 00:54:24.809
Hello!

00:54:24.869 --> 00:54:27.060
Where are you going?

00:54:27.120 --> 00:54:29.973
It was Aurelius.

00:54:30.033 --> 00:54:33.566
I don't know, said Dorogen.

00:54:33.626 --> 00:54:36.738
My husband says I must leave him.

00:54:36.799 --> 00:54:42.602
The black rocks aren't there anymore, and I promise to be with you.

00:54:42.663 --> 00:54:46.094
Dorogen was very sad.

00:54:46.154 --> 00:54:49.775
Dorogen stopped speaking.

00:54:49.836 --> 00:54:55.318
And then something changed inside Aurelius' heart.

00:54:55.378 --> 00:54:58.950
"'I hate to see you this sad,' he said.

00:54:58.970 --> 00:55:02.322
"'Your husband is a good man.

00:55:02.382 --> 00:55:05.708
You and our irregulars have a perfect love.

00:55:05.768 --> 00:55:08.104
I must stop this.

00:55:08.164 --> 00:55:10.595
Go home to your husband.

00:55:10.655 --> 00:55:13.908
We'll forget about your promise.

00:55:13.968 --> 00:55:16.288
Thank you, Aurelius.

00:55:16.348 --> 00:55:17.689
Thank you.

00:55:17.749 --> 00:55:22.112
Oh, I'm so happy," said Dorogen.

00:55:22.172 --> 00:55:26.654
And then she went home to tell her husband.

00:55:26.714 --> 00:55:31.674
Then Aurelius remembered something.

00:55:31.734 --> 00:55:38.676
I have to pay Simon a thousand pounds, and I only have five hundred pounds.

00:55:38.736 --> 00:55:41.087
What am I going to do?

00:55:41.148 --> 00:55:44.660
I'll bring him five hundred pounds.

00:55:44.720 --> 00:55:47.602
I think he'll understand."

00:55:47.662 --> 00:55:51.716
Aurelius went back to Simon's house.

00:55:51.776 --> 00:55:54.638
Aurelius was very worried.

00:55:54.698 --> 00:55:58.992
Simon won't be very happy, he thought.

00:55:59.053 --> 00:56:02.216
Hello, said Simon.

00:56:02.276 --> 00:56:04.548
Do you have my money?

00:56:04.608 --> 00:56:09.792
I can give you five hundred pounds, said Aurelius.

00:56:09.852 --> 00:56:12.684
Why don't you pay me everything?

00:56:12.745 --> 00:56:16.017
I did everything you asked of me, didn't I?

00:56:16.077 --> 00:56:18.820
The black rocks disappeared.

00:56:18.880 --> 00:56:22.362
Yes, they did, said Aurelius.

00:56:22.422 --> 00:56:25.750
And I'm very sorry about the money.

00:56:25.810 --> 00:56:30.598
And then Aurelius told Simon everything.

00:56:30.658 --> 00:56:34.202
He told him about Dorogen and Arviragus.

00:56:34.262 --> 00:56:38.294
He told him about their perfect love.

00:56:38.355 --> 00:56:42.958
Your all very good people said the man.

00:56:43.018 --> 00:56:45.580
You did a very good thing.

00:56:45.640 --> 00:56:47.911
You have a good heart.

00:56:47.972 --> 00:56:50.808
And I want to be good as well.

00:56:50.868 --> 00:56:57.776
You forgot about Dorogen's promise, and so I'll forget about the thousand pounds.

00:56:57.837 --> 00:57:01.308
I won't take any money from you."

00:57:01.368 --> 00:57:05.542
Thank you, Simon, said Aurelius.

00:57:05.601 --> 00:57:09.134
And then Aurelius went home.

00:57:09.194 --> 00:57:13.376
I'll never be with Dorogen, he thought.

00:57:13.437 --> 00:57:18.832
But I'm happy, because I did a good thing.

00:57:18.892 --> 00:57:25.420
And that is the end of my story, said the Franklin.

00:57:25.480 --> 00:57:39.329
As you can see, it's different from the Merchant's story, because this story tells us that there are also many good people in the world.

00:57:39.389 --> 00:57:53.453
Chapter 6 The Pardoners Tale And now I have a story for you," said the partner to the other people in the group.

00:57:53.513 --> 00:57:56.874
It's a story about three men.

00:57:56.934 --> 00:58:02.335
They were called Amis, Lucian and Maurice.

00:58:02.395 --> 00:58:04.995
Amis talked a lot.

00:58:05.055 --> 00:58:08.386
The other two men didn't talk very much.

00:58:08.446 --> 00:58:11.656
These men were very bad.

00:58:11.716 --> 00:58:14.484
They only thought about money.

00:58:14.544 --> 00:58:19.353
They were always together, but they weren't friends.

00:58:19.413 --> 00:58:21.674
Friends help you.

00:58:21.734 --> 00:58:24.876
Friends listen to your problems.

00:58:24.937 --> 00:58:30.731
They were greedy, and they had no love in their hearts.

00:58:30.791 --> 00:58:34.804
I will begin my story in and in.

00:58:34.864 --> 00:58:41.012
The three men were together at a table near the window.

00:58:41.072 --> 00:58:45.747
I'm hungry," said Amis.

00:58:45.807 --> 00:58:48.938
So am I, said Lucian.

00:58:48.998 --> 00:58:51.288
I want something to eat.

00:58:51.348 --> 00:58:55.150
But then Amis saw something strange.

00:58:55.210 --> 00:58:57.070
Look, he said.

00:58:57.130 --> 00:58:58.940
Look out of the window.

00:58:59.000 --> 00:59:01.882
What are those two men doing?

00:59:01.942 --> 00:59:05.422
Oh, yes, said Lucian.

00:59:05.482 --> 00:59:07.990
They're carrying a man.

00:59:08.050 --> 00:59:11.138
You're right, said Amis.

00:59:11.198 --> 00:59:12.629
Who is he?

00:59:12.689 --> 00:59:14.650
I think we know him.

00:59:14.710 --> 00:59:17.720
Yes, it's Adranos.

00:59:17.780 --> 00:59:20.871
Inkeeper, said Amis.

00:59:20.931 --> 00:59:23.222
Is that Adranos?

00:59:23.282 --> 00:59:25.462
Yes, it is.

00:59:25.522 --> 00:59:28.343
Adranos died last night.

00:59:28.403 --> 00:59:32.874
Somebody killed him, said the Inkeeper.

00:59:32.934 --> 00:59:35.865
Who did this to Adranos?

00:59:35.925 --> 00:59:37.543
Asked Amis.

00:59:37.603 --> 00:59:41.742
Death did it, said the innkeeper.

00:59:41.803 --> 00:59:43.353
Death?

00:59:43.414 --> 00:59:46.735
That's a strange name, Zedamis.

00:59:46.795 --> 00:59:49.596
Why is he called death?

00:59:49.656 --> 00:59:54.628
Because of the things he does, said the innkeeper.

00:59:54.688 --> 01:00:00.070
Last week he met five people, and he killed them all.

01:00:00.130 --> 01:00:02.602
Nobody can find him.

01:00:02.662 --> 01:00:06.181
Everybody is worried about death.

01:00:06.241 --> 01:00:09.980
We'll look for him," said Amis.

01:00:10.040 --> 01:00:12.301
It'll be good fun.

01:00:12.361 --> 01:00:18.583
We'll find him, and we'll fight this strange man called Death.

01:00:18.644 --> 01:00:22.275
Don't do it, said the innkeeper.

01:00:22.335 --> 01:00:24.846
He's very dangerous.

01:00:24.906 --> 01:00:26.597
Don't worry.

01:00:26.657 --> 01:00:30.330
We know what to do, said Amis.

01:00:30.390 --> 01:00:36.564
People say that death lives near the mountain, said the innkeeper.

01:00:36.624 --> 01:00:43.255
Don't go near the mountain, or you'll be the next people to die.

01:00:43.316 --> 01:00:47.077
Well, we're going to the mountain.

01:00:47.137 --> 01:00:49.418
Nothing will stop us.

01:00:49.478 --> 01:00:57.591
And so the three men left the inn, and then they started walking to the mountain.

01:00:57.651 --> 01:01:01.433
The three men walked for a long time.

01:01:01.493 --> 01:01:04.054
They often had to stop.

01:01:04.114 --> 01:01:09.286
After some hours, the three men met an old man.

01:01:09.346 --> 01:01:13.188
Hey, old man, said Amis.

01:01:13.248 --> 01:01:16.950
What do you want, said the old man?

01:01:17.010 --> 01:01:20.461
Do you know a man called Death?

01:01:20.521 --> 01:01:25.113
Yes, I know about him, said the old man.

01:01:25.173 --> 01:01:28.110
But why are you asking me this?

01:01:28.170 --> 01:01:30.777
Don't go near that man.

01:01:30.837 --> 01:01:32.728
He's dangerous.

01:01:32.788 --> 01:01:36.772
Tell us where we can find him, said Amis.

01:01:36.832 --> 01:01:41.826
Nobody knows where he is, said the old man.

01:01:41.886 --> 01:01:46.190
But people say he often goes to a place.

01:01:46.250 --> 01:01:49.944
They say he puts his money there.

01:01:50.004 --> 01:01:53.006
Money, said Amis.

01:01:53.067 --> 01:01:55.606
Where is this place?

01:01:55.666 --> 01:02:01.416
Before you walk up the mountain, there's a very old tree.

01:02:01.476 --> 01:02:05.268
It's near the road that goes to the mountain.

01:02:05.328 --> 01:02:08.170
Sometimes he goes there.

01:02:08.230 --> 01:02:12.062
They say he's got a lot of money.

01:02:12.122 --> 01:02:17.065
I think I know where this tree is, said Amis.

01:02:17.125 --> 01:02:19.546
We can go there now.

01:02:19.607 --> 01:02:21.618
No, stop!

01:02:21.678 --> 01:02:23.618
said the old man.

01:02:23.678 --> 01:02:26.265
But it was too late.

01:02:26.325 --> 01:02:30.742
The friends wanted to find the tree.

01:02:30.802 --> 01:02:39.566
After two hours, they arrived at the place, and they saw the tree.

01:02:39.627 --> 01:02:43.968
I want to look for the money now, said Amis.

01:02:44.028 --> 01:02:45.579
Do you remember?

01:02:45.639 --> 01:02:49.400
The old man said the desk put it here.

01:02:49.460 --> 01:02:54.256
They looked for the money, and soon they found it.

01:02:54.316 --> 01:02:57.392
It was under a small rock.

01:02:57.452 --> 01:03:01.276
There was a lot of money in a big bag.

01:03:01.336 --> 01:03:05.560
The bag was very difficult to carry.

01:03:05.620 --> 01:03:07.542
Here it is.

01:03:07.602 --> 01:03:09.674
Look how much there is.

01:03:09.734 --> 01:03:12.416
We're rich, Sidamis.

01:03:12.476 --> 01:03:14.669
Hooray, they said.

01:03:14.729 --> 01:03:17.192
We've got a lot of money.

01:03:17.252 --> 01:03:20.656
They were very excited.

01:03:20.716 --> 01:03:25.462
I want to get something to eat and drink," said Amis.

01:03:25.522 --> 01:03:28.214
Okay, said Lucian.

01:03:28.274 --> 01:03:31.557
We can go to the town and buy something.

01:03:31.617 --> 01:03:34.780
But wait, said Amis.

01:03:34.840 --> 01:03:38.002
Two of us must wait here with the money.

01:03:38.062 --> 01:03:40.914
Maurice, you go to the town.

01:03:40.975 --> 01:03:43.717
We'll wait for you here."

01:03:43.777 --> 01:03:49.446
Okay, said Maurice, and he went to the town.

01:03:49.506 --> 01:03:54.002
The other two men waited under the tree.

01:03:54.062 --> 01:03:58.693
After an hour, Amis thought of something.

01:03:58.753 --> 01:04:01.424
Listen, said Amis.

01:04:01.484 --> 01:04:04.925
There's a lot of money in that bag.

01:04:04.985 --> 01:04:08.356
Yes, you're right, said Lucian.

01:04:08.416 --> 01:04:11.296
There's about six hundred pounds.

01:04:11.357 --> 01:04:14.748
That's two hundred pounds each.

01:04:14.808 --> 01:04:16.490
Yes.

01:04:16.550 --> 01:04:21.486
But I think we can have 300 pounds each."

01:04:21.546 --> 01:04:22.916
How?

01:04:22.976 --> 01:04:24.598
said Lucian.

01:04:24.658 --> 01:04:32.183
Well, we can kill Maurice when he comes back, then we'll have more money.

01:04:32.244 --> 01:04:37.628
Yes, I want to do that, said Lucian.

01:04:37.688 --> 01:04:41.982
And then the two men waited for Maurice.

01:04:42.042 --> 01:04:45.553
Maurice was near the town.

01:04:45.613 --> 01:04:48.683
And he started thinking.

01:04:48.744 --> 01:04:54.366
Well, there's about 600 pounds in that bag.

01:04:54.426 --> 01:04:57.508
That's about 200 pounds for me.

01:04:57.528 --> 01:05:01.930
200 pounds is a lot of money.

01:05:01.990 --> 01:05:06.382
But 600 pounds is much more.

01:05:06.442 --> 01:05:10.594
600 pounds will change my life.

01:05:10.654 --> 01:05:13.057
I know what I'll do.

01:05:13.117 --> 01:05:19.473
I'll kill Amis and Lucian, then I'll have all the money."

01:05:19.533 --> 01:05:24.937
Ten minutes later, Maurice arrived at the town.

01:05:24.997 --> 01:05:31.672
He bought some food and drink, but he also bought some poison.

01:05:31.732 --> 01:05:37.988
He put the poison in the drink, and then he went back to the tree.

01:05:38.048 --> 01:05:42.034
It was getting late when Maurice arrived.

01:05:42.094 --> 01:05:56.688
Amis, Lucian, I've got the food, and they were the last words that Maurice spoke, because then Amis and Lucian killed him.

01:05:56.748 --> 01:06:02.210
And now we have more money, said Amis.

01:06:02.270 --> 01:06:06.104
They didn't worry about Maurice.

01:06:06.164 --> 01:06:09.416
The two men were happy.

01:06:09.476 --> 01:06:11.938
They drank together.

01:06:11.998 --> 01:06:15.880
Soon the poison was in their bodies.

01:06:15.940 --> 01:06:21.326
And after one minute, the poison killed them.

01:06:21.386 --> 01:06:26.330
That's the end of my story, said the partner.

01:06:26.390 --> 01:06:30.323
The three men wanted to fight death.

01:06:30.383 --> 01:06:32.534
They were greedy.

01:06:32.594 --> 01:06:35.928
And that's why they died.

01:06:35.988 --> 01:06:41.375
I want you to remember this story when we arrive at Canterbury.

01:06:41.436 --> 01:06:45.212
and when we say our prayers.

01:06:45.272 --> 01:06:49.606
The others thought it was a very good story.

01:06:49.666 --> 01:06:54.392
And then the people in the group thought about all the stories.

01:06:54.452 --> 01:06:58.045
There were a lot of things to think about.

01:06:58.106 --> 01:07:04.362
And, after four days, Canterbury was very, very near.

